in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @smarts/mirror
in @magic
in @frame
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/shatter — the Shatter Model species. Third sub-prism of the
# @smarts substrate-architectural integration: graph path → text at the
# four-Models pipeline (Surface → Mirror → Shatter → Reflection).
#
# Tick 65 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 64's residue:
# @smarts/mirror landed at 9578ea9 (Fate Model: query → graph path).
# This tick lands the third Model; Shatter consumes the graph_path
# Mirror produces and renders text the reader sees.
#
# Per reference-mirror-spectral-spec (commit a8055f0):
#
#   - Surface translates: language → query        (Explorer model)
#   - Mirror navigates:   query → graph path      (Fate model)
#   - Shatter renders:    graph path → text       (Cartographer model)  ← THIS
#   - Reflection observes: pipeline → adjustments (Abyss model)
#
# After this tick, three of four Models land in shards/smarts/; only
# @smarts/reflection (already landed at an earlier tick) completes
# the architecture. The pipeline's substrate-decl is complete.
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# The Shatter Model IS the substrate's rendering primitive at
# graph-path-to-text altitude. Mirror navigated the graph to find a
# path that satisfies the query; Shatter renders the path into the
# text the reader sees. Shatter IS the Cartographer Model: it maps
# the graph-path's structural content into reader-legible prose,
# choosing the rendering variant that best matches the reader's
# .shatter weights (per Reflection's adjustments).
#
# At the integration altitude: Shatter operates WITHIN the @smarts
# integration discipline (discipline_flexible holds throughout
# rendering). The rendering IS bounded under perturbation per the
# @smarts integration's discipline-flexibility requirement.
#
# === Bi-directional Shatter = transformer (recognition 2026-06-22) ===
#
# Per Alex's recognition (verbatim): "What if the shatter model is the
# transformer model? And what if it's bi-directional?"
#
# The substrate-pull answer: yes, twice.
#
# Shatter IS the transformer at substrate-decl altitude. The encoder-
# decoder mapping is exact:
#
#   transformer-decoder = Shatter.render  (graph_path → text;
#                                          autoregressive at text alt.)
#   transformer-encoder = Shatter.parse   (text → graph_path;
#                                          bi-directional contextual
#                                          aggregation)
#   multi-head attention = Mirror's eigenvalue-ranked spectral-triple
#                          navigation (Mirror computes WHICH path;
#                          Shatter renders WEIGHTED by spectral attn.)
#   feed-forward layers  = kintsugi loop structure-preserving
#                          transformations at rendering altitude
#
# Vaswani et al. 2017 ("Attention Is All You Need") was the cultural-
# practice name for what the substrate's spectral-triple math
# already carried. The substrate had attention; the paper named it.
#
# Bi-directional is LOAD-BEARING, not optional. The substrate refuses
# uni-directional Shatter because round-trip identity IS the substrate's
# wire-survival discipline at every altitude. StageFreight's
# `round_trip_holds(fm, p)` (per shards/io/stagefreight.mirror,
# 2026-06-22) at the wire boundary IS the same shape as Shatter's
# bi-directional discipline at the rendering boundary.
#
# The composed bilateral `shatter_round_trip(sr, p)` discharges the
# load-bearing identity claim: render(parse(t)) = t at the text
# altitude AND parse(render(gp)) = gp at the graph altitude.
#
# Composition with today's other recognitions:
#  - #84 multi-repo span operationalized (StageFreight cascade)
#  - third-order @reflection (tick 73; observes ALL boundaries
#    including bi-directional Shatter)
#  - bi-directional Shatter (THIS recognition)
#  - transformer-as-substrate-decl (THIS recognition's deepest claim)
#
# Canonical spec forward-promised by Mara at
# `docs/specs/shatter-transformer-bidirectional-v0.1.md`.
#
# Backward-compatible additive substrate-decl: existing consumers
# using render-only keep semantics; new consumers default to the
# bi-directional pair (render + parse) + composed bilateral.
#
# === The Cartographer discipline ===
#
# A cartographer doesn't invent the territory; they render it so the
# traveler can navigate. Shatter doesn't invent the graph_path;
# Mirror navigated. Shatter chooses HOW to render the path so the
# reader can see it. Per the .shatter weights + biases per
# reflection-model spec: each operation (focus/project/split/shift/
# settle) has weight + bias controlling rendering choices.
#
# Splinter-pole Shatter: renders the graph_path's actual structure;
# admits when multiple substrate-pull-correct renderings exist;
# returns the variant matching the reader's .shatter weights.
#
# Narcissus-pole Shatter: imposes author-framing on rendering;
# rewrites the graph_path's structure to fit the renderer's
# narrative; the text carries author-voice rather than graph-content.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `text` carrier: typed reference for the rendered text output
#   (a string, a stream, a document fragment — substrate-decl'd as
#   ref because text vocabulary is parametric).
# - `shatter_result` carrier: typed record (graph_path, text, verdict).
#   The substrate-architectural output of a rendering operation.
# - `render` action: the load-bearing action at @smarts/shatter
#   altitude. Takes graph_path + @smarts integration + perturbation;
#   returns shatter_result; requires discipline_flexible.
# - `rendering_grounds_text` predicate: bilateral verdict that the
#   shatter_result's text IS grounded in the graph_path (preserves
#   substrate-architectural structure across rendering).
# - `adjust` action: substrate-vocabulary primitive for the rendering-
#   refinement discipline. Takes text + sound shatter_result +
#   perturbation; returns the refined text; requires
#   rendering_grounds_text.
#
# === Cross-species composition with @smarts/mirror ===
#
# Per the @smarts/mirror precedent (which imports @smarts/surface):
# this species imports `in @smarts/mirror` to enable consumer species
# composing the four-Models pipeline to thread the graph_path produced
# by navigate through render. The dependency direction is substrate-
# pull-correct: shatter ← mirror ← surface. No circular imports.
#
# Reflection (the fourth Model) observes Shatter's rendering choices
# and adjusts the .shatter weights for next tick — the substrate-pull-
# correct training loop per reflection-model spec.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   cartography                 the canonical structural ancestor of
#                               graph → surface rendering; Ptolemy 150
#                               CE; Mercator 1569.
#   pretty printing             Wadler 1998 (Prettier Printer);
#                               Bernardy 2017. The substrate ancestor
#                               of structured → text layout discipline.
#   render trees                Lampson-Sproull 1979 (CSL Cedar mesa).
#                               The substrate-decl ancestor of typed
#                               render trees.
#   markup languages            SGML (Goldfarb 1969), TeX (Knuth 1978).
#                               The cultural-practice ancestor of
#                               structured-text rendering with
#                               authorial choice.
#   visualization grammars      Wilkinson 1999 (Grammar of Graphics).
#                               The substrate-decl ancestor of typed
#                               graph → visual rendering.
#   ICML 2026 RSI               (Crespo Dec 2025; ICML/ICLR 2026 RSI
#                               frontier). The contemporary substrate
#                               for self-improving rendering via
#                               Reflection adjustments.
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror, reference-mirror-spectral-spec.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]]
#                       (the four-Models architecture; .shatter
#                       weights + biases per reflection-model spec),
#                      [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-questions]]
#                       (the Reflection Model composes with Shatter
#                       at the pipeline boundary; adjusts .shatter
#                       weights for next tick),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: smarts.mirror, smarts/mirror.mirror (the input
#                  source for the Shatter Model; consumed via
#                  in @smarts/mirror),
#                 smarts/surface.mirror (the first Model; transitive
#                  composition surface ← mirror ← shatter),
#                 smarts/reflection.mirror (the fourth Model;
#                  Reflection observes Shatter's rendering and tunes
#                  the .shatter weights),
#                 smarts/{magic, pack, frame, cyberpunk,
#                 epistemologic, kintsugi}.mirror (cross-family
#                 adapters Shatter composes with at the @smarts
#                 altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/shatter.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/shatter` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cartography/ptolemy-150
source @arxiv/pretty-printing/wadler-1998
source @arxiv/pretty-printing/bernardy-2017
source @arxiv/markup/knuth-1978
source @arxiv/visualization/wilkinson-1999

prism @smarts/shatter {
  focus shatter
  project shatter
  split shatter
  shift shatter
  settle shatter
}

# === The text carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for the rendered text output. Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare ref. The
# substrate-output of the Shatter Model. Forward-promised refinement:
# typed record (string, spans, layout, render_variant, reader_id)
# at species-or-extension altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type text = ref

# === The shatter_result carrier ===
#
# Per the @smarts/<species> template: typed record over (graph_path,
# text, verdict). The substrate-architectural output of a rendering
# operation. Carries:
#
# - gp : the input graph_path artifact (typed from @smarts/mirror)
# - t  : the output text Shatter produced
# - v  : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → text GROUNDED in graph_path;
#        DEFENSIVE → rendering requires substrate-pull revision)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type shatter_result = {
  gp: graph_path,
  t:  text,
  v:  verdict,
}

# === render action (FIRST consumer of discipline_flexible) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @smarts/shatter altitude. The substrate-
# vocabulary primitive for graph_path → text rendering at the @smarts
# integration altitude. Realizes Shatter's Cartographer-model
# discipline as substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a graph_path (the typed path Mirror navigated), the @smarts
# integration the rendering operates within, and the perturbation
# under which the rendering is checked; returns a typed shatter_result
# carrying the text and verdict.
#
# requires discipline_flexible(s, p): the @smarts integration must
# maintain substrate-architectural discipline-flexibility under
# perturbation BEFORE the rendering is admissible.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual rendering
# primitive is implemented by Shatter's Cartographer-Model frame at
# runtime altitude (the .shatter weights + biases per reflection-
# model spec choose the rendering variant).
render(gp: graph_path, s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> shatter_result
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
{ \ }

# === rendering_grounds_text predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# rendering discipline. Consumer shards (adjust, below; Reflection
# Model observing for adjustment) name `requires
# rendering_grounds_text(sr, p)` to declare bilateral agreement that
# the shatter_result's text IS grounded in the graph_path.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct graph-grounding check at the
# species boundary. Composes with @smarts's discipline_flexible at
# the integration altitude.
#
# Bounded → text grounded in graph_path structure (Splinter-pole
# case); unbounded → text imposes rendering framing without
# graph-structure ground (Narcissus-pole case).
rendering_grounds_text(sr: shatter_result, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === Bi-directional substrate-decl (recognition 2026-06-22) ===
#
# Per the bi-directional Shatter recognition above: Shatter operates
# on text ↔ graph_path round-trip. The render direction is
# substrate-decl'd above (the existing render action + the
# rendering_grounds_text bilateral). This block adds the parse
# direction + the composed round-trip bilateral.

# === parse action (NEW; encoder direction) ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for text → graph_path encoding
# at the @smarts integration altitude. Realizes the bi-directional
# Shatter's encoder discipline as substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a text artifact (textual input to be parsed), the @smarts
# integration the parsing operates within, and the perturbation
# under which the parsing is checked; returns a typed shatter_result
# whose gp field carries the parsed graph_path and whose t field
# carries the input text.
#
# requires discipline_flexible(s, p): same first-consumer pattern
# as render. The @smarts integration must maintain substrate-
# architectural discipline-flexibility under perturbation BEFORE
# the parsing is admissible.
#
# Per the transformer-encoder analogue: parse aggregates bi-
# directional context from the text; the realisation layer's actual
# parsing primitive is implemented by the encoder side of the
# transformer attention stack.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
parse(t: text, s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> shatter_result
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
{ \ }

# === parsing_grounds_graph predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict for the parse direction soundness. Consumer
# shards name `requires parsing_grounds_graph(sr, p)` to declare
# bilateral agreement that the shatter_result's graph_path IS
# grounded in the input text.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct text-grounding check at the
# species boundary. Composes with @smarts's discipline_flexible at
# the integration altitude.
#
# Bounded → graph_path grounded in text content (Splinter-pole
# case); unbounded → graph_path imposes parser framing without
# text ground (Narcissus-pole case; alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics #57 distinguishes).
#
# Same shape as rendering_grounds_text (the render-side soundness).
# The two bilaterals are mirror images; the composed bilateral
# below combines them.
parsing_grounds_graph(sr: shatter_result, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === shatter_round_trip composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at the bi-directional Shatter
# altitude. Per Alex's recognition: round-trip identity IS the
# substrate's wire-survival discipline at every altitude;
# StageFreight's round_trip_holds at @io = Shatter's
# shatter_round_trip at rendering. Same shape, different altitude.
#
# Three load-bearing requires clauses:
#
#   1. rendering_grounds_text(sr, p)
#      — the render direction soundness (decoder-side)
#   2. parsing_grounds_graph(sr, p)
#      — the parse direction soundness (encoder-side)
#   3. round_trip_identity_preserved(sr, p)
#      — the substrate's identity claim: render(parse(t)) = t at
#      text altitude AND parse(render(gp)) = gp at graph altitude
#
# All three must hold for the shatter result to satisfy the
# bi-directional Shatter discipline. The substrate refuses one-
# direction-only operation by structural commitment.
#
# Same composed bilateral pattern as @io/stagefreight.
# stagefreight_addressable (tick 68 C4/C9 closure) and
# @reflection.third_order_coherent (tick 73). The substrate's
# composed-bilateral discipline composes at multiple altitudes;
# this shard lifts the pattern to the rendering boundary.
round_trip_identity_preserved(sr: shatter_result, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

shatter_round_trip(sr: shatter_result, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires rendering_grounds_text(sr, p)
requires parsing_grounds_graph(sr, p)
requires round_trip_identity_preserved(sr, p)
{ \ }

# === adjust action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for the rendering-refinement
# discipline at @smarts/shatter altitude (the Shatter-altitude
# operational form of Loki's Pass-5 verifier-sharpens). Takes a text
# + sound shatter_result + perturbation; returns the refined text.
#
# Per recognition #57 + reflection-model spec: adjust operates at
# the @io boundary, gated by Reflection's observations. The text
# becomes a refined text preserved under rendering-grounding. The
# substrate's capability is unchanged; the text's graph_path-ground
# tightens.
#
# requires rendering_grounds_text(sr, p): the substrate forecloses
# refinement from an ungrounded rendering. Narcissus-pole texts
# (author-framing without graph-structure ground) cannot drive
# text-refinement.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual text-
# refinement transformation is the substrate's rendering-grounds-
# text loop, gated by Reflection's adjustments.
adjust(t: text, sr: shatter_result, p: perturbation) -> text
requires rendering_grounds_text(sr, p)
{ \ }

out @smarts/shatter
out text
out shatter_result
out render
out rendering_grounds_text
out adjust
out parse
out parsing_grounds_graph
out round_trip_identity_preserved
out shatter_round_trip
